WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:09.719
The controls are NIST special publication
eight hundred fifty-three controls in its

3
00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:14.151
Moderate baseline: C M six,
C A seven, A C two, A C six,

4
00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:19.400
S A eleven, C M seven, S I seven,
A U three, C M three and C M five.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.414
A check is monitoring evidence only
if it can't change what it reads,

6
00:00:23.414 --> 00:00:25.312
and can't pass when it didn't look.

7
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:28.125
The run's validation
results show that an AD

8
00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:31.250
object can't take over a
cloud account unnoticed.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.680
A deviation is approved,
documented, and has an end:

10
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.612
the window date in the run's
options, and its change record.

11
00:00:38.612 --> 00:00:43.696
Least privilege: no standing Global
Administrator identity for a scheduled check,

12
00:00:43.696 --> 00:00:47.674
shown by the evidence block that
says the read came from an export.

13
00:00:47.674 --> 00:00:52.300
The test results, including the safety
tests, show the kit can only read.

14
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.600
In Lab 2, the validation manifest
holds a hash for every file of the run.

15
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.863
And the remediation is a write under
change control, never the check.

16
00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:06.773
The Key Security Indicators come from
FedRAMP's Key Security Indicators list,

17
00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:10.399
FedRAMP 20x indicators for
cloud service providers.

18
00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:14.020
Which output supports which
control is this workbook's reading.
